1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,433
AI agents have become remarkable writing partners.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:11,033
In a code editor, they read a whole project, make precise edits, and check their own work.

3
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:16,033
But most of the writing that matters doesn't live in a code editor.

4
00:00:16,133 --> 00:00:18,467
It lives on the page.

5
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:23,000
This is Inline.

6
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:32,900
Inline is a paginated document editor with Claude Code and Codex built in.

7
00:00:32,967 --> 00:00:38,367
The agent works on the same page you do, through more than forty document tools.

8
00:00:38,433 --> 00:00:42,533
And every edit it makes is a suggestion you can review.

9
00:00:42,633 --> 00:00:45,367
It's free, and open source.

10
00:00:49,300 --> 00:00:55,500
It runs as a desktop app on Mac, Windows, and Linux, with everything included.

11
00:00:55,567 --> 00:00:57,900
Let's open a real account.

12
00:01:01,100 --> 00:01:02,633
This is home.

13
00:01:02,733 --> 00:01:08,267
Documents live in color-coded folders, with live previews of their pages.

14
00:01:08,367 --> 00:01:14,300
Templates cover essays, MLA papers, reports, résumés and more.

15
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:18,167
And search finds any document in a keystroke.

16
00:01:23,100 --> 00:01:27,033
Open a thesis proposal and you get real pages.

17
00:01:27,133 --> 00:01:35,167
A live table of contents, citations, LaTeX equations, tables and figures, with headers and page numbers.

18
00:01:35,233 --> 00:01:38,467
Everything you'd expect from a word processor.

19
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:48,500
Press Command J, and Claude joins you.

20
00:01:48,567 --> 00:01:51,400
Ask it to tighten the introduction.

21
00:01:51,467 --> 00:01:55,433
Claude reads the document and edits the page directly.

22
00:01:55,500 --> 00:02:02,333
Every change appears as a tracked suggestion: deletions struck through, additions highlighted.

23
00:02:02,433 --> 00:02:06,300
It even noticed a citation that doesn't match its source.

24
00:02:06,367 --> 00:02:12,400
Keep what you like and undo the rest, one change at a time, or all at once.

25
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:24,233
Select a passage and press Command L to ask about just that part.

26
00:02:24,333 --> 00:02:32,667
Here, Claude checks the claim against the paper, finds the right hurricane, and rewrites the sentence, with its sources.

27
00:02:41,100 --> 00:02:43,600
Comments work the way you'd expect.

28
00:02:43,700 --> 00:02:46,200
My advisor left three.

29
00:02:46,267 --> 00:02:53,500
Ask Claude to address them, and it fixes each one in the text, replies in the thread, and resolves it.

30
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:07,433
Save named versions as you go, and open any earlier draft to compare it or restore it.

31
00:03:07,533 --> 00:03:11,633
Every reply from the agent leaves a restore checkpoint, too.

32
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:16,800
Prefer Codex?

33
00:03:16,900 --> 00:03:20,833
Switch providers or models in the middle of a conversation.

34
00:03:20,933 --> 00:03:25,200
The next model picks up the same transcript, and the same document.

35
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:32,133
When the layout is part of the message, use a Canvas.

36
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:40,400
The agent designs editable pages with columns, color, and type, and you can still click in and change any word.

37
00:03:45,100 --> 00:03:50,900
Import a PDF, and Inline matches its page size, fonts, and margins.

38
00:03:50,967 --> 00:04:00,433
Then Claude rebuilds each page as editable text, with equations in LaTeX, and checks its work against the original, side by side.

39
00:04:08,100 --> 00:04:13,800
Back home, Organize with AI files everything into folders in seconds.

40
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:19,267
It reads only titles and first lines, so it barely touches your usage.

41
00:04:23,100 --> 00:04:25,767
Your documents stay yours.

42
00:04:25,867 --> 00:04:37,233
Inline keeps a Word copy of every one in a folder on your computer, exports to PDF, Markdown and more, and brings in your whole Google Drive from a single zip.

43
00:04:41,100 --> 00:04:47,767
And because Inline speaks MCP, Claude Code in your terminal can work on your documents too.

44
00:04:47,867 --> 00:04:52,200
Ask from the command line, and watch the edit land on the page.

45
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:01,800
Inline.

46
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:05,433
Real documents, with the agent built in.

47
00:05:05,533 --> 00:05:09,933
Free and open source, for Mac, Windows, and Linux.
